lens:
READER-2 (my draft for PREREG-EVL-10). It is a new reader version: frozen prompts with their own shas, claude-sonnet-5-5, structured outputs, streamed, effort "low". It reads only the eligible, liquid (adv20 >= $10M), TRADABLE, v1-rank-top subset (v1 score >= 2, issuers sampled by hash) that one consumer seat's 8 slots can trade: about 39-50 reads a session. It is registered together with that seat, EVL-R2-ON (close of D to the open of D+1), and the seat's control, before any READER-2 read of any event exists. Its fields are frozen now as FEATURES-R2 v1, which later learner and meta-learner versions may take only through a later file, all columns or none. A smoke test of at most $0.01 runs before the freeze.

I started from the EVL-7 reader lens's sketch (evl7/EDGE-RESULT.json design-reader) and the judge's NOT TAKEN note. I changed it where the code, the frozen PREREG-EVL-6 screen, the budget, PREREG-EVL-8's timing table and PREREG-EVL-7's E8 and E10 guards force a change. The main changes:
- one model, not a Haiku/Sonnet cascade;
- one seat, not two;
- no earnings-release reads;
- the consumer is decided at 15:40 ET so it fits the close late pass;
- the guards are written into the record, so the record is what money can buy.

Every file is in ~/Work/.ltcm-main/goal-2026-10-19/evl10/reader2/, with sha256 values in SHA256SUMS:
- r2_spec.py: the frozen texts, schemas, shas, parser and set rules;
- cost_r2.py with cost_r2.out;
- smoke_r2.py, which only ran as a dry run (smoke_r2.dry.out);
- calib_r2.py with calib_r2.{null,power,stress,power2,final}.jsonl and their logs;
- ev_r2.py with ev_r2.out;
- budget_r2.py with budget_r2.out;
- evl6_frozen/: PREREG-EVL-6's calib_final.py, calib_v2.py and search_final.py, byte-identical to docs/prereg/evl-6/SHA256SUMS.

design:
A. WHAT THE CODE SAYS TODAY (rel/1019h, read only)
- v1 verdicts (verdicts.py):
  - PROMPT-DOC and PROMPT-NEWS, Haiku 4.5, temperature 0, 300 tokens;
  - programs read score >= 2, score 3, and guidance raised with score >= 1;
  - book.picks ranks by (rank_key, adv20 desc), so a READ row's real money takes the LARGEST names among about 54-165 score >= 2 ties a session (SPEED-FACTS);
  - "price target" is in 1,117 of the 4,346 headlines (HOUSE-FACTS).
- Prices (gateway CLAUDE_MODELS):
  - Sonnet 5.5: $2 in, $2.50 5-minute write, $10 out a million tokens;
  - Opus 5.5: exactly 2x that;
  - both geo us 1.1;
  - admit() allows thinking adaptive with display, output_config {effort, format json_schema} and stream.
- gw.post_stream exists (1019h, built for the Opus births call).
- The lane's line is $3 a UTC day (house.py VERDICT_USD_DAY), shared by verdicts and births; the House's fixed cost is about $1.25 (A87).
- The news table holds headline, summary, symbols and source only (no body).
- The replay charges 5 bp impact a side at adv20 >= $10M and 10 bp below it (score.py LIQUID_ADV), so liquid names cost about 10 bp less a round trip.

B. CHANGES TO THE EVL-7 SKETCH, AND WHY
1. ONE MODEL, claude-sonnet-5-5, for every read. There is no Haiku tier and no cascade; the lens asks for a stronger model, and the slots fix the read count.
2. Earnings 8-Ks (item 2.02) are NOT read.
   - At the open: every pre-open earnings issuer is ERN(D). PREREG-EVL-7's E8 (followed by EVL-8 and EVL-9) bars an open-to-close row from it, because selling at D's close takes the name from EVL-5's and EVL-2's close rows through the book's sale gate.
   - At the close: an earnings consumer would need the lane's 15:30 reaction mark, which is fetched only inside the 15:47 close run. By PREREG-EVL-8's timing table that is too late for the 15:48 late-pass tick, and the DROP, UNDER and REACT rows take the reaction bands first.
   - So the EVL-7 lens's EDGAR previous-release fetch is dropped too.
   - "Surprise against the company's own previous guidance" and "consensus language" are read where the texts state them: earnings articles ("beats $X estimate", "raises FY outlook") and 8.01/7.01 outlook updates.
3. ONE SEAT, EVL-R2-ON. EVL-R2-O1 is fully specified as an option but not recommended now. Four reasons:
   - (a) budget: LEFT before this file is 0.78 with no birth and 0.39 with A104's three (budget_r2.out), and EVL-11 and R3 compete for it;
   - (b) literature: buying at the open after attention-grabbing news pays the opening premium, which reverses intraday (Berkman, Koch, Tuttle and Zhang 2012, JFQA 47(4)), while overnight returns carry the attention and momentum premium (Lou, Polk and Skouras 2019, JFE 134(1));
   - (c) cost halves: $0.41 against $0.54 a day mid (cost_r2.out);
   - (d) at 8 picks a session PREREG-EVL-6 promotes slowly at any edge below about 60 bp (section C), so a second seat at the weak auction costs more charge than it adds expected passes.
4. JUDGED EQUALS TRADED.
   - E10 (the next-open 8-K guard) and PREREG-EVL-4's EXCLUDED(D) are part of the candidate definition, so the shadow record never holds a name the guards bar from money.
   - The shadow is exactly the top-8 picks, the order real money takes.
5. LIVE-ONLY RECORD. No READER-2 read can exist before the code ships, so there is no catch-up. The record's clock starts at the first live decision after the release. For this file code speed is clock speed (unlike PREREG-EVL-7 to -9).
6. TIMING THAT NEVER DELAYS AN EARLIER FILE.
   - The consumer is decided at 15:40:00 ET (tau), from rows stored before it, in its own SQL-only run that yields to every lane task.
   - Its buys are planned in the book's close LATE PASS at the 15:48 tick, after every row of PREREG-EVL-1 to -9 planned at or before that tick.
   - Day news is knowable to T29 (15:29), so reads have about 10 minutes after the last article.

C. THE READ SET (THE "RANK-TOP SUBSET THE SLOTS CAN TRADE")
- NEWS-ON: articles of EVL-NEWS-READ-ON's family for D (single-symbol, knowable after 09:00 ET of D and by T29) that meet all of:
  - a stored ok PROMPT-NEWS score >= 2;
  - the issuer is live-eligible for D and TRADABLE;
  - adv20 >= $10M.
- How issuers are chosen:
  - every issuer whose best qualifying v1 score is 3 is read;
  - a score-2 issuer is read when h = sha256("R2|ON|D|cik") < q;
  - q = min(1, 40 / the mean qualifying-issuer count of the last 5 complete sessions), and 0.5 before any session is complete;
  - at most 2 reads an issuer: its first qualifying article, and a later one with a higher v1 score;
  - hard cap 64 reads a session.
- 8K-ON: 8-Ks of EVL-8K-READ-ON's family F8K(D) (items 1.01, 2.01, 7.01 or 8.01, no 2.02, D's close window, issuer not EXCLUDED(D)) whose v1 PROMPT-DOC verdict is ok with score <= 1. These are names no earlier close row takes. All are read, cap 8.
- NEWS-ON is made of DAY(D) issuers and 8K-ON of non-DAY(D) issuers, so the two never share an issuer.
- EXPECTED READS A SESSION (SPEED-FACTS counts x an unknown liquid share of 0.4 / 0.6 / 0.8): news 31.8 / 37.2 / 42.0 and 8-K 7.4 / 8.0 / 8.0 (cost_r2.out on_only, Oct 20-21). That is about 39-50 reads. The count follows the slots, not the news volume: a 2,255-article day costs about what a 917-article day costs.

D. WHAT A READ SEES (r2_spec.py)
- NEWS:
  - symbol, the universe name, created ET, source, headline and summary;
  - up to 40 lines "date ET | source | headline" of stored articles naming the ticker in the 30 days before the item (received before the ask);
  - up to 10 lines of the issuer's stored 8-Ks with their items.
- DOC (8-K): v1's document TEXT (first 16,000 characters, the same document sha) plus up to 25 news lines (30 days before the filing up to the ask).
- No market data is given. Stored headlines may mention prices, as v1's do. The store's news begins Oct 19, so the 30 days are shorter until about Nov 18, and prior_n records the lines given.
- NEWS schema (10 fields):
  - type (13 values);
  - new 0-2 (novelty against the 30 days);
  - corroborated 0-2 (confirmation across sources or the company's own filing);
  - price_story;
  - consensus (beat / inline / miss / mixed / not_stated, as stated);
  - vs_own_guidance (9 values, as stated);
  - magnitude 0-3, specific 0-2, surprise -3..3;
  - p_up 0-100 in steps of 5 (direction with its confidence).
- DOC schema (15 fields): the news fields with "routine" in place of price_story, plus material 0-3 (8-K item materiality), guide_chg_pct, dilution, one_offs and tone -2..2.
- Schema rules: integers are enums, nullable numbers are anyOf, additionalProperties false, every field required.
- Prompt shas (sha256 of the canonical spec, recomputed at the freeze): R2-NEWS 617f8979922b38f3fc5e95f1a2c830b4c02a248131d6865b9ad20c3c390a11be, R2-DOC 65d79226d019cce1ce7e249553f225781ecb85e74960b3a323c35f8e7914e650.

E. THE SEAT
EVL-R2-ON v1 is seatable from its first live decision, at learning size.
- Buys at the CLOSE of D, sells at the OPEN of D+1 (hold 1). Tau is 15:40:00 ET.
- Candidates: the ON SET's issuers with an ok read answered before tau, not barred by E10 (any 8-K of the issuer knowable from 09:00 ET of D, stored before tau, with v1 ok score >= 2, or score >= 1 with guidance raised, or no answer), not EXCLUDED(D) for the 8K-ON part, TRADABLE, and knowable after REGISTERED_AT_10. Each issuer's best read counts.
- Filter: all of
  - not a price story, routine filing, dilution or investor materials;
  - type not price_move or commentary;
  - vs_own_guidance not below, lowered or withdrawn;
  - consensus not miss;
  - new >= 1, surprise >= 1, p_up >= 60.
- Ranking: p_up, then surprise, magnitude, specific and corroborated, then the lower h.
- Picks: the top 8 not held within 5 sessions (A72), with rank_key = 9 - position.
- Control: EVL-R2-ON-SET, a free record of every candidate.
- Rules shared with other files:
  - PREREG-EVL-2's limit at entry;
  - the replay (PREREG-EVL-1 section 5);
  - judged by PREREG-EVL-6 sections 1-3 as frozen;
  - Probe and Sized by PREREG-EVL-6 section 6 (A99); 8 picks bound every band;
  - ROOM after every row of PREREG-EVL-1 to -9 and before R3's births, planned in the late pass and keeping no room.

F. LINES AND COST
- Every R2 dollar counts in the lane's line.
- A call is sent only while both hold:
  - the lane's line left after the call's worst-case hold is >= $1.00 (v1 first);
  - R2's day spend plus the hold is <= $0.75 a UTC day.
- Worst-case holds are $0.055 a news read and $0.103 a doc read (cost_r2.out).
- Mid cost is $0.41 a day: 10.3 bp of a Probe lot, or 17.9 bp of a learning lot, at 6 buys a session. Section events_per_session_and_cost has the full range.

G. FEATURES-R2 v1 AND LATER FILES
- The feature map is frozen here and written once per (event, decision) from rows stored before tau. It holds:
  - the one-hot enums and the ordinal fields scaled;
  - the booleans;
  - guide_chg_pct clipped, with a null indicator;
  - kind, ln(1 + prior_n) and latency;
  - r2_missing.
- A later file may give a NEW VERSION of a PREREG-EVL-7 or -9 learner, or a PREREG-EVL-8 meta-learner, these columns: all or none, never chosen after outcomes exist, with its own registration time, charge and screen.
- EVL-R2-ON is decided at 15:40 in its own run before EVL-META-ON's decision. Under PREREG-EVL-8 section 7.2 as written it is then an ordinary hold-1 source (a program expert p:EVL-R2-ON:1, asleep until MINB 3 settled blocks; 2 experts, inside the 1,535 cap). PREREG-EVL-8's text binds that reading. This file registers no free single-field R2 records, so R2's fields reach the meta-learners only through a later file.

H. RS-2 (A REPORT ONLY)
- It reports forward, on the SET record's settled outcomes:
  - the Spearman IC of p_up and surprise against v1's score;
  - an issuer-block bootstrap CI of IC(p_up) - IC(v1);
  - the top-8 lift;
  - missing and cost shares.
- It is for the captain and the owner only: on births' FACTS_DENY and the report's designer deny list. Nothing follows from it automatically.

I. SMOKE TEST (smoke_r2.py), at most $0.01, before the freeze
- Two streamed Sonnet 5.5 calls with R2's exact body shape on pinned synthetic texts (ticker ZZXQ, a company that does not exist):
  - DOC schema, max_tokens 400, worst case $0.0077;
  - NEWS schema, max_tokens 300, worst case $0.0060; sent only if call 1's stated cost + $0.0060 <= $0.01.
- PASS needs all of: the gateway admits the body, both answers parse ok, and the ltcm.cost event arrives. The measured tokens are recorded in the registering amendment.
- If output_config.format is refused, R2-J (the same texts plus a JSON-only line, no format) is pinned before the freeze. A "max_tokens" stop is a finding, not a fail.
- Dry run: doc body 4,540 bytes, news 3,466 (smoke_r2.dry.out). The captain runs --send; I sent nothing.

why_it_compounds:
1. THE SLOTS BIND (A94), SO THE KEY IS THE LEVER.
   - A seat's profit a session is the edge of the 8 events it fills. Its key decides that edge (Grinold 1989, JPM 15(3)).
   - Today v1's 7-level score with an ADV tie-break gives a READ row's real money the 8 largest of 54-165 ties.
   - In calib_r2 a continuous key beat a coarse v1-like 3-level key with size ties at the same information: +1.5 against -3.6 bp a pick at sd 0.8%, c 0.3, n26 (calib_r2.power.jsonl).
   - A filter made of the reader's own fields doubled the edge against a random filter: +27.5 against +9.8 bp at c 0.5 (calib_r2.power2.jsonl).
   - Reading 40 issuers instead of 24 added about 10 bp (37.9 against 27.5 bp, power2).
2. THE FIELDS THE LITERATURE PRICES, STORED WRITE-ONCE WITH KNOWABLE TIMES. FEATURES-R2 v1 (frozen now) turns every session's 39-50 read events into labelled rows for later learner and meta-learner versions. The all-or-nothing rule means no designer picks a field after outcomes exist. The fields and their literature:
   - novelty and staleness: Tetlock 2011, RFS 24(5); Fedyk and Hodson 2023, JFE 149(1);
   - news versus no-news drift: Chan 2003, JFE 70(2);
   - analyst actions and targets: Womack 1996, JF 51(1); Brav and Lehavy 2003, JF 58(5);
   - consensus surprise: Bernard and Thomas 1989, JAR 27;
   - guidance: Anilowski, Feng and Skinner 2007, JAE 44;
   - 8-K item materiality: Lerman and Livnat 2010, RAST 15(4);
   - LLM reading of headlines: Lopez-Lira and Tang 2023, arXiv:2304.07619.
3. MORE SEATED, JUDGED CAPITAL (A118). One more seat holds up to 8 learning lots (about $300 at $38) the moment its code is live, judged forward.
4. COST FOLLOWS THE SLOTS, NOT THE FEED. The hash share caps reads near 40 news a session whatever the volume. R2's $0.75 line and the $1.00 v1 reserve keep v1 first.
5. A CLEAN FORWARD TEST OF READING QUALITY. The control is the same v1 >= 2 liquid set, so "beats its control" is exactly the claim that the stronger reader adds information over v1. RS-2 measures it for the owner without any designer seeing it.
6. NO CONTAMINATION. Every event postdates the model's training (Glasserman and Lin 2023, arXiv:2309.17322).
7. AGAINST IT:
   - LLM news predictability concentrates in small stocks and negative news, which a long-only, $10M-ADV seat can use only by avoidance (Lopez-Lira and Tang);
   - published effects decay (McLean and Pontiff 2016, JF 71(1)).
